{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/934253-advantages-granted-to-a-pack-by-a-totem","id":934253,"title":"Advantages granted to a Pack by a Totem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-19T20:11:38-07:00","id":934253,"title":"Advantages granted to a Pack by a Totem","content":"What do you consider acceptable for a viable advantage granted to a pack by a Fox Totem Rank3 ( Perception rank 2 / Wisdom Rank 1) ?<br /> <br /> In the section on advantages, it is written that a Totem can grants many thing, but interestingly, they do not grant Gifts/Facets.<br /> <br /> Would that be a viable idea or would it screw something that im not aware ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T23:34:43-07:00","id":934314,"title":"","content":"Also, do you think that if I rename the merit Aura Reading and transform it into a specific ability, it can be fitting ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T00:42:20-07:00","id":934337,"title":"","content":"I think you may have left something out in your first post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T01:33:52-07:00","id":934350,"title":"","content":"There are a couple reasons I can think of that Totems don't grant gifts/facets in 2e.<br /> <br /> One, is that learning a gift is carving it into your soul, it's painful and instinctive and becomes fundamental to the Uratha's being. So having it as a benefit granted to you by a totem doesn't make sense narratively. It's not just some knowledge or blessing that a totem can bestow or take away from you as it pleases. Otherwise it would be carving and recarving your very being as it did so.<br /> <br /> Two, it's a bit of a mess mechanically. Not all werewolves will have the renown of whatever Facet the totem grants, making it likely that many Facets would be effectively useless (and again, not thematic, considering the role of renown re: gifts) on half the pack. Especially for those that scale on renown. <br /> <br /> It's also strange because there are a quite a few hidden benefits in granting a facet flat out. It unlocks a gift, which is a benefit of somewhere between 1, 3 and 5 experience, despite the fact that a facet itself is worth only 2 experience (if the gift is already unlocked). So that's a hard balance call. So it'll be worth more or less to certain characters depending on their gift affinities and whether they have it unlocked or not.<br /> <br /> I personally would have no objection to a totem granting Supernatural merits, however. After all it claims to bypass prerequisites and many of them can make for interesting benefits. I've even been conceiving of a poor, poor pack bound to some Luck or Gambling totem that confers the Thief of Fate merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T02:33:43-07:00","id":934364,"title":"","content":"This is a very good summary reasoning why not, Amravanti.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T12:17:57-07:00","id":934644,"title":"","content":"Well, Amravanti, you put things clearly in perspective. Thanks alot, it helped me.<br /> <br /> <br /> So now im still thinking about my Totem Watch-Fox the Wise. Since he represent perception il all its form, including introspection, and wisdom... I was thinking about him granting something similar to aura reading... wich is not by extend something too far fetched, since those supernatural merits are tied to humans. However it cost 3. Alternatively, just a dot in Wits would be helpful, but then, it cost 4, and I still have 1 XP to buy something tied to perception/wisdom.<br /> <br /> At least im far less confused. I remember too much Werewolf the Forsaken first edition. There are so many differences now. I must read more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T14:35:25-07:00","id":934711,"title":"","content":"You could have it offer Aura Reading and a dot in Investigation. Or a point of Wits and a Skill Specialty in Investigation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T14:38:08-07:00","id":934713,"title":"","content":"And don't forget the Trained Observer merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T15:04:52-07:00","id":934721,"title":"","content":"Excatly that nofather. I was thinking about Aura reading and a dot in Investigation or Empathy... or a speciality in Empathy like &quot;motives&quot;, or a skill specialty in Investigation. Trained Observer is a great merit too that I was considering. Too many option now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the way, I have 2 other questions that you might be able to answer if you like of course.<br /> <br /> 1- Is there a way for an Uratha to communicate like... always communicate, regardless of distance or the side of the gauntlet your are, with his totem... like telepathy ? I read somewhere before, that some storyteller do exactly this. It might be fun, but then, I also read that it would only be plausible with a specific totem related to communication or something similar. What are your personal view or interpretation of the game on this ?<br /> <br /> 2- Can the facet of a specifi gift be used to replace a numina that a spirit would otherwise have ?<br /> <br /> So far you have been really helpful.<br /> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","user":"Warriorshaman","date":". 07-20-2016, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T15:24:06-07:00","id":934730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/934253-advantages-granted-to-a-pack-by-a-totem?p=934721#post934721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- Is there a way for an Uratha to communicate like... always communicate, regardless of distance or the side of the gauntlet your are, with his totem... like telepathy ? I read somewhere before, that some storyteller do exactly this. It might be fun, but then, I also read that it would only be plausible with a specific totem related to communication or something similar. What are your personal view or interpretation of the game on this ?</div> </div> </div> </div>There should be a numina for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/934253-advantages-granted-to-a-pack-by-a-totem?p=934721#post934721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2- Can the facet of a specifi gift be used to replace a numina that a spirit would otherwise have ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Gifts are nowadays exclusively tied to Renown, which Spirits lack entirely. You'll notice certain numina or dread powers that work akin to some facets without depending on them, such as Labyrinth.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}